// BEGIN TIMESHEET RULES
    // Heartwood timesheets carry no companyId (unchanged). Everyone else's must name their own company,
    // so Heartwood never sees them and their own admins can.
    // One diff, reused: each extra diff of the entries/edits maps counts against the 1000-expression limit.
    // A machine pick is written once, all three fields together.
    // An existing shift: check only what changed. id, source, author, enteredAt and the clock-on stamp never change;
    // a recorded stamp or machine pick is never rewritten or removed; a new stamp is a valid fix taken now (clock shifts only).
    // Re-validating the whole shift on every tap pushed clock-off after a break past Firestore's 1000-expression limit
    // (permission-denied, user test 11 Nov 2026).
    // Clock-off after a break and a machine pick used to hit Firestore's 1000-expression limit (permission-denied):
    // the entries map was diffed three times and compared whole. Diff once and look the shift up once.

    match /timesheets/{id} {
      function incAdminOf(c) {
        return incStaffOf(c) && get(/databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(request.auth.uid)).data.get("role", "") == "admin";
      }
